#
# ---- A BUILD DEFECT NEARLY BURIED THIS FIX: no header dependencies ----
# First measurement after (o) read: storport total_functions 1620 -> 1207,
# hardware 93 -> 5, port_io 20 -> 0, slot_hits 2030 -> 159, and ACPI's report
# failing to parse.  That looked like a catastrophic pipeline regression.
# It was not (o).  `grep -c "include/.*\.h" Makefile` returned ZERO: the object
# rule had no header dependencies at all, so widening x86_operand_t.disp from
# int32_t to int64_t left already-built objects linked against the OLD struct
# layout.  The mixed binary decoded every instruction after the first as "???"
# at address 0.  Every unit suite passed throughout, because each test target
# compiles its sources directly on every run; only the LINKED binary was mixed,
# and only the linked binary is what the differential and the report use.
# Diagnosed by measuring rather than reasoning: the decoder's own walk was
# fine and IMPROVED (storport nostart 76 -> 2, addr 28 -> 0) while the
# pipeline's disassembly began at "1c0001000: ???" and then ran at address 0.
# Fix: -MMD -MP on the object rule and -include of the generated .d files.
# CONTROLS, run to prove the dependency fires rather than assuming it:
#   touch include/x86_decoder.h  -> 4 objects recompile
#   no-op build                  -> 0 objects recompile
#   touch include/semantic.h     -> exactly translator.c and semantic.c
# (A first control run reported 0 and was RIGHT to: no .d files existed yet,
# because nothing had been compiled since the flag was added.)
#
# ---- OUTCOME after a clean build, every (o) prediction read ----
# hardware_functions: ACPI 47 -> 45 and storport 93 -> 85 EXACTLY as predicted,
#   and NO other input moved (HDAudBus 21, disk 3, i8042prt 31, pci 29,
#   HP serial 48, usbxhci 58; controls 9, 3, 0).
# port_io_functions: ACPI 13 -> 11, storport 20 -> 12 -- the 2 and 8 phantom
#   port operations are gone, exactly the ten located on 2026-09-20 as sitting
#   inside (o) desync runs with a moffs64 trigger.
# iat_slot_hits: storport 2030 -> 2031.  (o) also closed (a)'s ONE outstanding
#   miss: the site our walk never reached was hidden behind a moffs desync.
# test-x86 pass=93 xfail=19 fail=0 xpass=0; test-port-attestation 1/1 with 8
#   drivers analysed, 0 registered; test-semantic 38/38 of 0 registered;
#   both sweeps PASS with the reduced set; full make test exit 0, 25 suites.
